flowchart BT
    accTitle: Faultline architecture
    accDescr: On one machine, the CLI submits jobs and requests snapshots from a coordinator at 127.0.0.1:9000. The coordinator owns the FIFO queue, job state, and worker registry. Each worker connects independently, registers for an ID, receives assignments, reports job progress and outcomes, and sends a heartbeat every two seconds by default. Six seconds of heartbeat silence expires an assignment. The coordinator appends and syncs its local write-ahead log before acknowledging submissions, dispatching assignments, or publishing accepted results, and replays the log at startup.

    subgraph HOST["Faultline · local MVP"]
        direction BT
        CLI["CLI<br/>Submit jobs · inspect state"]
        C["Coordinator · 127.0.0.1:9000<br/>FIFO queue · job state · worker registry<br/>Heartbeat timeout: 6 s by default"]
        subgraph POOL["Independent workers"]
            direction LR
            W1["Worker 1<br/>One task at a time"]
            WN["Worker N<br/>One task at a time"]
            W1 ~~~ WN
        end
        WAL[("Local write-ahead log<br/>Jobs · results · retries<br/>Identity counters")]

        CLI -->|Submit / inspect| C
        C -->|ACK / reply| CLI
        C -->|Worker ID / assignments| POOL
        POOL -->|Register / job reports| C
        POOL -.->|Heartbeats / 2 s| C
        C -->|Append + sync| WAL
        WAL -->|Startup replay| C
    end

    classDef client fill:#f1f5f9,stroke:#64748b,color:#172033
    classDef coordinator fill:#eef2ff,stroke:#6366f1,color:#172033,stroke-width:2px
    classDef worker fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#172033
    classDef storage fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#172033
    class CLI client
    class C coordinator
    class W1,WN worker
    class WAL storage
